        "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
        "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued November 2 at 2:43AM PST until November 2 at 6:00PM PST by NWS San Diego CA",
        "description": "* WHAT...Elevated surf of 3-6 ft, and an afternoon high tide just\nover 6 feet will result in minor tidal overflow.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...Through this afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor tidal overflow and dangerous rip currents.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Today's high tide will occur around 3:30\nPM. Tides are expected to increase for the end of the week, with\ntides reaching 7 ft as early as Friday. Tides will peak over\nthe weekend into early next week around 7.5 ft. Reminder, tides\nmentioned have been corrected to reflect the current trends in\nactual tide observations.",
